{"agent_id":"pp3g-7zcB-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-3470","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:45:52.838188338Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1601ce29-9575-4697-bf0c-60e15b30cc67","comment_uuid":"48cd443e-1007-417d-b8de-95b5aadabf9d","author":"pp3g-7zcB-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-3470","content":"VERDICT: CONDITIONAL\n\n## Summary\nThe Observer v1 implementation (scripts/observer/observer.sh + tests/run-tests.sh) delivers the complete feature set specified in .design/lifecycle-manager-design.md (SC1-SC5), the #460 dispatch plan (M1 R1-R4, M2 F1-F6), and .crosslink/knowledge/data-retention.md. All six verdict transitions (COMPLETED, FINISHED-UNMARKABLE, FAILED, KILLED, PARKED, FROZEN) are implemented with correct scoped actions. Wave-level actions (merge detection, doctrine DIS validation, admission checks, wave anomaly) are present. F1-F6 features are fully implemented. Test suite passes 97/98 (1 failure is test-environment: issue #460 not locked in this session).\n\nHowever, several correctness and operational risks require remediation before production deployment.\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### CRITICAL\n\n**1. Missing  in bash wrapper (observer.sh:167)**\nOnly  is set. Command failures in the bash loop (mkdir, cat, python3 invocations, sleep) will not terminate the script, causing silent continuation with corrupted state. The python  function handles subprocess errors, but the bash wrapper does not.\n- Evidence: line 167 only has ; lines 2447-2488 show unchecked command substitutions\n- Impact: A failed  (line 300, suppressed with 2>/dev/null) or  could leave the observer in an undefined state\n\n**2. Unbounded growth of state files — no rotation/cleanup (observer.sh:297, 395-398, 1067)**\n-  (line 297): appended every cycle, never rotated\n-  (line 396): appended on every transition, never rotated\n-  (line 398): appended, never cleaned\n-  (line 1067): appended, never cleaned\n-  directories (line 695): created per transition, never pruned\n-  cache (line 1678): entries expire but dict grows until cleanup pass\n-  (line 475): entries expire after 1h but list accumulates\n- Impact: In a long-running deployment (days/weeks), /tmp/opencode/observer-state/ will fill disk\n\n**3. State directory creation suppresses errors (observer.sh:300)**\n — permission failures (e.g., /tmp mounted noexec, uid mismatch) are silent. Subsequent writes fail mysteriously.\n- Evidence: line 300\n\n**4. Unused  parameter in  function (observer.sh:436)**\nParameter accepted but never used. Dead code suggests incomplete error-handling design.\n- Evidence: line 436 defines ; never referenced in function body\n\n---\n\n### MAJOR\n\n**5.  reads entire index file into memory (observer.sh:1956-1960)**\n\nIndex files grow with every exported session row. For large deployments (10k+ sessions), this could OOM the observer process.\n- Evidence: lines 1956-1960\n- Fix: Stream hash via e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855  - or read in chunks\n\n**6.  regex may miss valid model declarations (observer.sh:2172-2176)**\nPatterns:\n-  — misses quoted values \n-  — misses YAML quoted strings \n-  — greedy, may capture false positives in prose\n- Evidence: lines 2172-2176; admission_checks at 2229-2234\n\n**7.  regex assumes specific comment format (observer.sh:768-770)**\n\nCrosslink comments may have different timestamp formats or kind labels. If format changes, hub position becomes None silently.\n- Evidence: lines 768-770\n\n**8.  limited pattern coverage (observer.sh:587-615)**\nOnly matches:\n-  (with specific spacing)\n-  (seconds)\n- \nMisses ISO timestamps with seconds, RFC3339, or  HTTP header formats.\n- Evidence: lines 590-614\n\n**9. Bash wrapper  quoting risk (observer.sh:2475)**\nCYCLE_PROG is a single-quoted heredoc containing single quotes. Passing via  risks quote nesting issues if the heredoc content changes.\n- Evidence: line 2475; CYCLE_PROG defined at line 330 with  (single-quoted)\n\n**10.  only tracks liveness script, not python program failures (observer.sh:2455-2463, 2476-2482)**\nPython program failures (prog_rc != 0) are logged but don't increment the consecutive error counter. The cap at line 2460 only triggers on liveness failures.\n- Evidence: lines 2455-2463 vs 2476-2482\n\n---\n\n### MINOR\n\n**11. Evidence bundles never cleaned (observer.sh:695)**\n — accumulates indefinitely. No retention policy for Observer's own evidence artefacts.\n- Evidence: line 695; data-retention.md only covers session data, not Observer evidence\n\n**12. No explicit umask/permissions for state files in /tmp (observer.sh:300, 459-463)**\nState files created with default umask. In multi-user /tmp, other users could read/write observer-state/.\n- Evidence: line 300 (mkdir), lines 459-463 (atomic write)\n\n**13.  no structure validation (observer.sh:2447-2449)**\n\nInvalid JSON passes to python program which then fails at json.load (line 2321), but the error is generic.\n- Evidence: lines 2447-2449, 2321-2325\n\n**14.  returns None on git errors, treated as fresh (observer.sh:678-688, 1252-1265)**\nIf 1787620984 fails (rc != 0 or non-numeric output), returns None. In  (line 1252),  skips commit-overdue check entirely — a git error looks like a fresh commit.\n- Evidence: lines 684-687, 1252-1265\n\n**15.  scans entire doc universe every cycle (observer.sh:1431-1447, 1554-1603)**\n walks  and  up to 800 files. Runs every cycle (120s default). Expensive for large repos.\n- Evidence: lines 1431-1447 (build_doc_universe), 1554 (wave_doctrine called every cycle)\n\n**16.  only checks for / tables (observer.sh:1827-1841)**\nIf opencode adds  or renames columns, exports silently skip those tables. No alert on schema drift.\n- Evidence: lines 1831-1838\n\n**17.  uses lexicographic sort on timestamps (observer.sh:1810-1824)**\n — assumes timestamp prefix sorts correctly. If stamp format changes, wrong generation pruned.\n- Evidence: lines 1814-1818\n\n---\n\n## WHY / WHAT / HOW-CERTAIN / WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n\n**WHY**: The code correctly implements all specified behaviours (6 verdicts, 4 wave actions, F1-F6 features) and passes the matched-pair test suite. The architecture is sound: out-of-process, state-owned, crosslink-only mutations, evidence-hashed transitions. The CONDITIONAL verdict reflects operational risks (unbounded growth, missing set -e, memory risk in rclone cat) that will cause production incidents if deployed as-is.\n\n**WHAT**: 17 findings (4 CRITICAL, 5 MAJOR, 8 MINOR) with file:line evidence above. All are fixable without architectural changes.\n\n**HOW-CERTAIN**: Evidence-based for all findings. Code read completely; test suite executed (97/98 pass); specs cross-referenced. The T16 test failure is confirmed environment-related (issue #460 not locked), not a code defect.\n\n**WHAT-NOT-TESTED**:\n- Non-dry-run mutations end-to-end (crosslink kickoff stop/cleanup, issue comments) — orchestrator validates at shakedown n=1 per #460 handoff\n- Real rclone remote sync (OBSERVER_RCLONE_REMOTE unset in test env; negative path tested, positive path not)\n- Long-duration loop behaviour (interval gating, consecutive error cap, circuit breaker over hours)\n- RED verification branch fault injection (code path inspected only)\n- Multi-agent concurrent transitions (tests are sequential fixtures)\n- Schema drift in opencode.db (session_v3, column changes)\n- Large index file rclone cat memory pressure (not load-tested)","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:45:52.831656917Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:Pd4zv+GGjayCUcQ4RSMbR4zvUXkTPGJnOKdDIekPvhI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg6BwqNXyUq4w+onrNWbuNif0yTKwg3P0ei/hALw7cqeIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAcSj/1AMuSerYYBg9H8YDdAeKVBI6JjtfgVDErf/loHJii8u0+8nS1qOY8IlwSbxQnJ/w/BJJr3ILyvBW6inSBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Pd4zv+GGjayCUcQ4RSMbR4zvUXkTPGJnOKdDIekPvhI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3